IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- SCHEDULE 6B -- CHANGES IN CONTROL OF REGISTERED CRYPTOASSET BUSINESSES (S.I. 2017/692, lines 3391-3543 of the
-- plain-text rendering, which is not the official text and is not verified against it).
--
-- WHAT IT IS FOR.  Part 12 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (FSMA) makes a person who acquires, increases
-- or reduces control over an authorised firm tell the regulator first, and lets the regulator object.  This Schedule
-- extends Part 12 to a cryptoasset exchange provider that is on the FCA's register (regulation 54(1A)), with changes:
-- the FCA is the regulator, the tests of "control" are replaced, some sections are switched off, and the offences
-- carry their own penalties and a defence.  Paragraphs 1 and 2 are for a business entered on the register BEFORE
-- 25 October 2027; paragraphs 3 and 4 for a business entered on or after that day; paragraph 5 defines terms.
--
-- WHAT IS AND IS NOT ENCODED (the Schedule changes another Act, so most of it is a list of changes to that Act's
-- sections, and the Act's own text is not among the sources).
--  * The changes themselves are a TABLE: one row for each lettered limb of paragraphs 2 and 4, naming the section of
--    Part 12 it changes and whether the limb switches the section off ("disregarded"), replaces it with text set out in
--    the limb, or changes some of its words.  A function answers, for a section, how the Schedule treats it.
--  * Where a limb SETS OUT operative text, that text is encoded as a rule: sections 181, 182 and 183 (what acquiring,
--    increasing, reducing and ceasing to have control are), section 186 (the one assessment criterion), section 191B(3ZA)
--    (the FCA's direction against a beneficial owner), section 191F(8) to (10) (penalties and a defence) and the
--    definition inserted into section 191G.
--  * The unamended text of Part 12 is NOT here.  A section that no limb mentions is reported as "not mentioned", not as
--    applying or not applying.
--
-- WHICH SET OF CHANGES APPLIES depends on the date the business was entered on the register: the Schedule's own words,
-- not a date of the person asking.  The text does not say when Schedule 6B itself comes into force (the dates in
-- October 2027 are dates of registration), so no rule here turns on "today".  Both sets are encoded (FORK S6B-F2).  The split is a date the text fixes in its own words: a registered
-- cryptoasset business included on the wrong side of it makes paragraph 1 (or 3) answer JUST FALSE, read like a period (FORK S6B-F4, assumed, not ruled).
--
-- INPUTS BORROWED FROM ELSEWHERE.  "Beneficial owner within the meaning of regulation 5 or 6" is asked as a MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- (SEAM S-K2, asking: the keel answers it).  "Fit and proper person within the meaning of regulation 58A", "included in the
-- register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)" and "cryptoasset exchange provider / custodian wallet provider within
-- the meaning of regulation 14A" are answered by other parts (mlr3, mlr1) in sections the register of seams does not list for
-- this Schedule; they are taken as inputs here and proposed as new seams in NOTES.md.  Percentages of shares and voting power
-- are NUMBERs (0 to 100).  "Parent undertaking" and "significant influence over the management" are undefined here and are
-- taken as BOOLEAN facts.
--
-- THE TEXT SAYS DIFFERENT THINGS IN PLACES THAT LOOK ALIKE (FINDINGS in NOTES.md, none corrected here).
--  * Paragraph 5 defines "registered cryptoasset business" as a cryptoasset EXCHANGE PROVIDER on the register; the definition
--    inserted into section 191G (lines 3492 and 3537) says an exchange provider OR a custodian wallet provider.  Paragraphs 1
--    and 3 speak in the Schedule's own words, so paragraph 5 governs them: a custodian wallet provider is not within them
--    (FORK S6B-F1).
--  * Section 183(3)(b)(i) (line 3439) says 10% of the shares "in B"; sections 181(1)(b)(i) and 183(3)(b)(ii) say "in B or P".
--  * The penalty for an offence under subsection (4) in Scotland and Northern Ireland is "the statutory minimum" in line 3485
--    and in both subsection (8)(a)(ii) texts, and "the statutory maximum" in line 3530 (FORK S6B-F3).

-- src:3391 | Schedule 6B — Changes in Control of Registered Cryptoasset Businesses
§ `Schedule 6B -- Changes in Control of Registered Cryptoasset Businesses`

DECLARE `sch 6B the set of modifications` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6B the modifications in paragraph 2`
    `sch 6B the modifications in paragraph 4`
    `sch 6B paragraphs 1 and 3 do not say that Part 12 applies`

DECLARE `sch 6B treatment of a section` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6B the section is disregarded`
    `sch 6B the section is replaced by the text set out`
    `sch 6B the section is read with the changes listed`
    `sch 6B the section is not mentioned in the modifications`
    `sch 6B no modification applies because paragraphs 1 and 3 do not say that Part 12 applies`

DECLARE `sch 6B modification` HAS
    `the section of Part 12 of FSMA`     IS A STRING
    `how the limb treats the section`    IS A `sch 6B treatment of a section`
    `what the limb does to the section`  IS A STRING

DECLARE `sch 6B reference in Part 12 of FSMA` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6B a reference to a UK authorised person`
    `sch 6B a reference to the appropriate regulator`
    `sch 6B a reference to each regulator`
    `sch 6B a reference to another term`

DECLARE `sch 6B what the reference is read as` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6B a registered cryptoasset business`
    `sch 6B the FCA`
    `sch 6B no reading is given by this limb`

-- A holding of shares or of voting power in the business or its parent undertaking, before and after the step being asked about.
DECLARE `sch 6B holding` HAS
    `the percentage before the step`  IS A NUMBER
    `the percentage after the step`   IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `sch 6B offence group` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6B an offence under section 191F(1) to (3) or (5) to (7)`
    `sch 6B an offence under section 191F(4)`
    `sch 6B an offence under another subsection of section 191F`

DECLARE `sch 6B mode of conviction` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6B summary conviction`
    `sch 6B conviction on indictment`

DECLARE `sch 6B penalty` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6B a fine`
    `sch 6B a fine not exceeding the statutory minimum`
    `sch 6B a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum`
    `sch 6B imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine, or both`
    `sch 6B the penalty is not stated in this paragraph`

-- Helper (not a provision): the answer to "A or B" when each is a MAYBE BOOLEAN.  JUST TRUE if either is JUST TRUE;
-- JUST FALSE only if both are JUST FALSE; otherwise NOTHING.
@ref sch 6B (helper for the limbs that join two beneficial-owner questions with "or")
GIVEN x IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      y IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF x EQUALS JUST TRUE OR y EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF x EQUALS JUST FALSE AND y EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): both operands are the text's own no, each carrying its own quoted words where it is answered
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an operand is a beneficial-owner answer (regulations 5 and 6, another part's) that the person could not give, and the other operand did not settle the matter

-- src:3392 | 1 Modifications: Control over registered cryptoasset businesses registered before 25th October 2027
-- src:3393 | Part 12 of FSMA (control over authorised persons) applies, with the modifications specified in paragraph 2, to a registered cryptoasset business that is included in the register before 25th October 2027 and to which Part 12 of FSMA would not otherwise apply.
@ref sch 6B para 1 (src:3392-3393)
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 6B para 1 the date before which the business must have been included in the register` MEANS Date 25 10 2027

@ref sch 6B para 1 (src:3393)
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS A DATE
      `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 1 Part 12 of FSMA applies to the business with the modifications specified in paragraph 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (`sch 6B para 5 the business is a registered cryptoasset business` `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the date on which the business was included in the register` LESS THAN `sch 6B para 1 the date before which the business must have been included in the register`
           AND (NOT `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     (`sch 6B para 5 the business is a registered cryptoasset business` `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (NOT (`the date on which the business was included in the register` LESS THAN `sch 6B para 1 the date before which the business must have been included in the register`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "included in the register before 25th October 2027" is a date the text fixes in its own words, read like a period, so a business included on or after that day is outside it (assumed, not ruled: FORK S6B-F4)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph applies Part 12 to a registered cryptoasset business included in the register before 25th October 2027 and to which Part 12 would not otherwise apply; "to which Part 12 of FSMA would not otherwise apply" is a relative clause with no "where" or "if", and the paragraph does not say that Part 12 does not apply to another business

-- src:3394 | The modifications specified in this paragraph are—
@ref sch 6B para 2 (src:3394)
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 6B modification`
`sch 6B para 2 the modifications` MEANS
    LIST `sch 6B para 2(c) section 178`
       , `sch 6B para 2(d) section 181`
       , `sch 6B para 2(e) section 182`
       , `sch 6B para 2(f) section 183`
       , `sch 6B para 2(g) section 184`
       , `sch 6B para 2(h) section 185`
       , `sch 6B para 2(i) section 186`
       , `sch 6B para 2(j) section 187`
       , `sch 6B para 2(k) section 187A`
       , `sch 6B para 2(l) section 187B`
       , `sch 6B para 2(m) section 187C`
       , `sch 6B para 2(n) section 189`
       , `sch 6B para 2(o) section 190`
       , `sch 6B para 2(p) section 190A`
       , `sch 6B para 2(q) section 191A`
       , `sch 6B para 2(r) section 191B`
       , `sch 6B para 2(s) section 191C`
       , `sch 6B para 2(t) section 191D`
       , `sch 6B para 2(u) section 191F`
       , `sch 6B para 2(v) section 191G`

-- src:3395 | (a) references to a “UK authorised person” are to be read as references to a registered cryptoasset business;
-- src:3396 | (b) references to “appropriate regulator” and “each regulator” are to be read as references to the FCA;
@ref sch 6B para 2(a) and (b) (src:3395-3396)
GIVEN `the reference in Part 12 of FSMA` IS A `sch 6B reference in Part 12 of FSMA`
GIVETH A `sch 6B what the reference is read as`
`sch 6B para 2(a) and (b) a reference in Part 12 of FSMA is read as` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reference in Part 12 of FSMA`
    WHEN `sch 6B a reference to a UK authorised person` THEN `sch 6B a registered cryptoasset business`
    WHEN `sch 6B a reference to the appropriate regulator` THEN `sch 6B the FCA`
    WHEN `sch 6B a reference to each regulator` THEN `sch 6B the FCA`
    WHEN `sch 6B a reference to another term` THEN `sch 6B no reading is given by this limb` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the limbs read three terms and name no other

-- src:3397 | (c) section 178 (obligation to notify the appropriate regulator: acquisitions of control) is to be read as if subsections (2ZA) and (2A) were omitted;
@ref sch 6B para 2(c) (src:3397)
GIVETH A `sch 6B modification`
`sch 6B para 2(c) section 178` MEANS
    `sch 6B modification` WITH
        `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS "178"
        `how the limb treats the section` IS `sch 6B the section is read with the changes listed`
        `what the limb does to the section` IS "subsections (2ZA) and (2A) omitted"

-- src:3398 | (d) section 181 (acquiring control) is to be read as if it said—
-- src:3399 | 181 Acquiring control
-- src:3400 | (1) For the purposes of this Part, a person (“A”) acquires control over a registered cryptoasset business (“B”) if, should the acquisition proceed—
-- src:3401 | (a) A would become a beneficial owner within the meaning of regulation 5 or 6 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 of—
-- src:3402 | (i) B; or
-- src:3403 | (ii) a parent undertaking of B (“P”); or
-- src:3404 | (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply A would—
-- src:3405 | (i) hold 10% or more of the shares in B or P;
-- src:3406 | (ii) hold 10% or more of the voting power in B or P; or
-- src:3407 | (iii) otherwise hold shares or voting power in B or P as a result of which A is able to exercise significant influence over the management of B.
@ref sch 6B para 2(d) (src:3398-3407)
GIVETH A `sch 6B modification`
`sch 6B para 2(d) section 181` MEANS
    `sch 6B modification` WITH
        `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS "181"
        `how the limb treats the section` IS `sch 6B the section is replaced by the text set out`
        `what the limb does to the section` IS "section 181 read as set out in the limb"

-- Section 181(1)(b), as set out in limb (d).  It applies if limb (a) does not; the caller below tries limb (a) first.
@ref sch 6B para 2(d) (src:3404-3407)
GIVEN `the percentage of the shares in the business that the person would hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the shares in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the voting power in the business that the person would hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the voting power in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the person would otherwise hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person is able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(d) section 181(1)(b) the person would hold the control described in limb (b)` MEANS
        `the percentage of the shares in the business that the person would hold` AT LEAST 10
     OR `the percentage of the shares in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` AT LEAST 10
     OR `the percentage of the voting power in the business that the person would hold` AT LEAST 10
     OR `the percentage of the voting power in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` AT LEAST 10
     OR `the person would otherwise hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person is able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business`

@ref sch 6B para 2(d) (src:3400-3407)
GIVEN `the person would become a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person would become a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the percentage of the shares in the business that the person would hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the shares in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the voting power in the business that the person would hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the voting power in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the person would otherwise hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person is able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(d) section 181 the person acquires control over the business` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` `the person would become a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` `the person would become a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR (`sch 6B para 2(d) section 181(1)(b) the person would hold the control described in limb (b)` `the percentage of the shares in the business that the person would hold` `the percentage of the shares in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` `the percentage of the voting power in the business that the person would hold` `the percentage of the voting power in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` `the person would otherwise hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person is able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     (`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` `the person would become a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` `the person would become a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND (NOT (`sch 6B para 2(d) section 181(1)(b) the person would hold the control described in limb (b)` `the percentage of the shares in the business that the person would hold` `the percentage of the shares in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` `the percentage of the voting power in the business that the person would hold` `the percentage of the voting power in the parent undertaking that the person would hold` `the person would otherwise hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person is able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person (“A”) acquires control over a registered cryptoasset business (“B”) if, should the acquisition proceed—" and neither limb (a) nor limb (b) is met (marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person would become a beneficial owner within regulation 5 or 6 is decided in that regulation, and limb (b) is not met

-- src:3408 | (e) section 182 (increasing control) is to be read as if it said—
-- src:3409 | 182 Increasing control
-- src:3410 | (1) For the purposes of this Part, a person (“A”) increases control over a registered cryptoasset business (“B”) if, should the increase in control proceed—
-- src:3411 | (a) A would become a beneficial owner within the meaning given by regulation 5 or 6 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 of—
-- src:3412 | (i) B; or
-- src:3413 | (ii) a parent undertaking of B (“P”); or
-- src:3414 | (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—
-- src:3415 | (i) the percentage of shares which A holds in B or P would increase by any of the steps mentioned in subsection (2);
-- src:3416 | (ii) the percentage of voting power A holds in B or P would increase by any of the steps mentioned in subsection (2); or
-- src:3417 | (iii) A becomes a parent undertaking of B.
-- src:3418 | (2) The steps are—
-- src:3419 | (a) from less than 20% to 20% or more;
-- src:3420 | (b) from less than 30% to 30% or more;
-- src:3421 | (c) from less than 50% to 50% or more.
@ref sch 6B para 2(e) (src:3408-3421)
GIVETH A `sch 6B modification`
`sch 6B para 2(e) section 182` MEANS
    `sch 6B modification` WITH
        `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS "182"
        `how the limb treats the section` IS `sch 6B the section is replaced by the text set out`
        `what the limb does to the section` IS "section 182 read as set out in the limb"

@ref sch 6B para 2(e) (src:3418-3421)
GIVEN holding IS A `sch 6B holding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(e) section 182(2) the percentage rises by one of the steps` MEANS
        (holding's `the percentage before the step` LESS THAN 20 AND holding's `the percentage after the step` AT LEAST 20)
     OR (holding's `the percentage before the step` LESS THAN 30 AND holding's `the percentage after the step` AT LEAST 30)
     OR (holding's `the percentage before the step` LESS THAN 50 AND holding's `the percentage after the step` AT LEAST 50)

@ref sch 6B para 2(e) (src:3414-3417)
GIVEN sharesInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      sharesInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      `the person becomes a parent undertaking of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(e) section 182(1)(b) the person would increase the holding described in limb (b)` MEANS
        `sch 6B para 2(e) section 182(2) the percentage rises by one of the steps` sharesInB
     OR `sch 6B para 2(e) section 182(2) the percentage rises by one of the steps` sharesInP
     OR `sch 6B para 2(e) section 182(2) the percentage rises by one of the steps` votingInB
     OR `sch 6B para 2(e) section 182(2) the percentage rises by one of the steps` votingInP
     OR `the person becomes a parent undertaking of the business`

@ref sch 6B para 2(e) (src:3410-3417)
GIVEN `the person would become a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person would become a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      sharesInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      sharesInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      `the person becomes a parent undertaking of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(e) section 182 the person increases control over the business` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` `the person would become a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` `the person would become a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR (`sch 6B para 2(e) section 182(1)(b) the person would increase the holding described in limb (b)` sharesInB sharesInP votingInB votingInP `the person becomes a parent undertaking of the business`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     (`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` `the person would become a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` `the person would become a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND (NOT (`sch 6B para 2(e) section 182(1)(b) the person would increase the holding described in limb (b)` sharesInB sharesInP votingInB votingInP `the person becomes a parent undertaking of the business`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person (“A”) increases control over a registered cryptoasset business (“B”) if, should the increase in control proceed—" and neither limb (a) nor limb (b) is met (marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person would become a beneficial owner within regulation 5 or 6 is decided in that regulation, and limb (b) is not met

-- src:3422 | (f) section 183 (reducing or ceasing to have control) is to be read as if it said—
-- src:3423 | 183 Reducing or ceasing to have control
-- src:3424 | (1) For the purposes of this Part, a person (“A”) reduces control over a registered cryptoasset business (“B”) if, should the decrease in control proceed—
-- src:3425 | (a) A would cease to be a beneficial owner within the meaning given by regulation 5 or 6 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 of—
-- src:3426 | (i) B; or
-- src:3427 | (ii) a parent undertaking of B (“P”); or
-- src:3428 | (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—
-- src:3429 | (i) the percentage of shares which A holds in B or P would decrease by any of the steps mentioned in subsection (2);
-- src:3430 | (ii) the percentage of voting power A holds in B or P would decrease by any of the steps mentioned in subsection (2); or
-- src:3431 | (iii) A ceases to be a parent undertaking of B.
-- src:3432 | (2) The steps are—
-- src:3433 | (a) from 50% or more to less than 50%;
-- src:3434 | (b) from 30% or more to less than 30%;
-- src:3435 | (c) from 20% or more to less than 20%.
-- src:3436 | (3) For the purposes of this Part, A ceases to have control over B if—
-- src:3437 | (a) A ceases to be a beneficial owner within the meaning given by regulation 5 or 6 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 of B or P; or
-- src:3438 | (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply, A ceases to be in the position of holding—
-- src:3439 | (i) 10% or more of the shares in B;
-- src:3440 | (ii) 10% or more of the voting power in B or P; or
-- src:3441 | (iii) shares or voting power in B or P as a result of which A is able to exercise significant influence over the management of B.
@ref sch 6B para 2(f) (src:3422-3441)
GIVETH A `sch 6B modification`
`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183` MEANS
    `sch 6B modification` WITH
        `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS "183"
        `how the limb treats the section` IS `sch 6B the section is replaced by the text set out`
        `what the limb does to the section` IS "section 183 read as set out in the limb"

@ref sch 6B para 2(f) (src:3432-3435)
GIVEN holding IS A `sch 6B holding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(2) the percentage falls by one of the steps` MEANS
        (holding's `the percentage before the step` AT LEAST 50 AND holding's `the percentage after the step` LESS THAN 50)
     OR (holding's `the percentage before the step` AT LEAST 30 AND holding's `the percentage after the step` LESS THAN 30)
     OR (holding's `the percentage before the step` AT LEAST 20 AND holding's `the percentage after the step` LESS THAN 20)

@ref sch 6B para 2(f) (src:3428-3431)
GIVEN sharesInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      sharesInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      `the person ceases to be a parent undertaking of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(1)(b) the person would decrease the holding described in limb (b)` MEANS
        `sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(2) the percentage falls by one of the steps` sharesInB
     OR `sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(2) the percentage falls by one of the steps` sharesInP
     OR `sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(2) the percentage falls by one of the steps` votingInB
     OR `sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(2) the percentage falls by one of the steps` votingInP
     OR `the person ceases to be a parent undertaking of the business`

@ref sch 6B para 2(f) (src:3424-3431)
GIVEN `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      sharesInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      sharesInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      `the person ceases to be a parent undertaking of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(1) the person reduces control over the business` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR (`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(1)(b) the person would decrease the holding described in limb (b)` sharesInB sharesInP votingInB votingInP `the person ceases to be a parent undertaking of the business`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     (`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND (NOT (`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(1)(b) the person would decrease the holding described in limb (b)` sharesInB sharesInP votingInB votingInP `the person ceases to be a parent undertaking of the business`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person (“A”) reduces control over a registered cryptoasset business (“B”) if, should the decrease in control proceed—" and neither limb (a) nor limb (b) is met (marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person would cease to be a beneficial owner within regulation 5 or 6 is decided in that regulation, and limb (b) is not met

-- Section 183(3).  Sub-paragraph (b)(i) says shares "in B" only, where (b)(ii) says voting power "in B or P" (FINDING in NOTES.md): read as printed.
@ref sch 6B para 2(f) (src:3438-3441)
GIVEN sharesInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      `the person ceases to hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person was able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(3)(b) the person ceases to be in the position described in limb (b)` MEANS
        (sharesInB's `the percentage before the step` AT LEAST 10 AND sharesInB's `the percentage after the step` LESS THAN 10)
     OR (votingInB's `the percentage before the step` AT LEAST 10 AND votingInB's `the percentage after the step` LESS THAN 10)
     OR (votingInP's `the percentage before the step` AT LEAST 10 AND votingInP's `the percentage after the step` LESS THAN 10)
     OR `the person ceases to hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person was able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business`

@ref sch 6B para 2(f) (src:3436-3441)
GIVEN `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      sharesInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInB IS A `sch 6B holding`
      votingInP IS A `sch 6B holding`
      `the person ceases to hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person was able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(3) the person ceases to have control over the business` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR (`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(3)(b) the person ceases to be in the position described in limb (b)` sharesInB votingInB votingInP `the person ceases to hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person was able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     (`sch 6B at least one of the two answers is yes` `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of the business within regulation 5 or 6` `the person would cease to be a beneficial owner of a parent undertaking of the business within regulation 5 or 6`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND (NOT (`sch 6B para 2(f) section 183(3)(b) the person ceases to be in the position described in limb (b)` sharesInB votingInB votingInP `the person ceases to hold shares or voting power in the business or its parent undertaking as a result of which the person was able to exercise significant influence over the management of the business`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of this Part, A ceases to have control over B if—" and neither limb (a) nor limb (b) is met (marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person would cease to be a beneficial owner within regulation 5 or 6 is decided in that regulation, and limb (b) is not met

