        `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS "191G"
        `how the limb treats the section` IS `sch 6B the section is read with the changes listed`
        `what the limb does to the section` IS "the definitions of 'the appropriate regulator', 'qualifying credit institution' and 'UK authorised person' omitted; a definition of 'registered cryptoasset business' inserted"

-- The definition inserted into section 191G by limb (v)(ii).  It names an exchange provider OR a custodian wallet provider (FORK S6B-F1).
@ref sch 6B para 2(v)(ii) (src:3492)
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is a custodian wallet provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 2(v)(ii) the business is a registered cryptoasset business within section 191G` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` OR `the business is a custodian wallet provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(2)`) AND `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registered cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider which is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)"

-- src:3493 | 3 Modifications: Control over registered cryptoasset businesses registered on and after 25 October 2027
-- src:3494 | Part 12 of FSMA (control over authorised persons) applies, with the modifications specified in paragraph 4, to a registered cryptoasset business that is included in the register on or after 25th October 2027 and to which Part 12 of FSMA would not otherwise apply.
@ref sch 6B para 3 (src:3493-3494)
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 6B para 3 the date on or after which the business must have been included in the register` MEANS Date 25 10 2027

@ref sch 6B para 3 (src:3494)
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS A DATE
      `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 3 Part 12 of FSMA applies to the business with the modifications specified in paragraph 4` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (`sch 6B para 5 the business is a registered cryptoasset business` `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the date on which the business was included in the register` AT LEAST `sch 6B para 3 the date on or after which the business must have been included in the register`
           AND (NOT `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     (`sch 6B para 5 the business is a registered cryptoasset business` `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (NOT (`the date on which the business was included in the register` AT LEAST `sch 6B para 3 the date on or after which the business must have been included in the register`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "included in the register on or after 25th October 2027" is a date the text fixes in its own words, read like a period, so a business included before that day is outside it (assumed, not ruled: FORK S6B-F4)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph applies Part 12 to a registered cryptoasset business included in the register on or after 25th October 2027 and to which Part 12 would not otherwise apply; "to which Part 12 of FSMA would not otherwise apply" is a relative clause with no "where" or "if", and the paragraph does not say that Part 12 does not apply to another business

-- src:3495 | The modifications specified in this paragraph are—
@ref sch 6B para 4 (src:3495)
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 6B modification`
`sch 6B para 4 the modifications` MEANS
    LIST `sch 6B para 4(c) section 178`
       , `sch 6B para 4(d) section 184`
       , `sch 6B para 4(e) section 185`
       , `sch 6B para 4(f) section 187`
       , `sch 6B para 4(g) section 187A`
       , `sch 6B para 4(h) section 187B`
       , `sch 6B para 4(i) section 187C`
       , `sch 6B para 4(j) section 189`
       , `sch 6B para 4(k) section 190`
       , `sch 6B para 4(l) section 190A`
       , `sch 6B para 4(m) section 191A`
       , `sch 6B para 4(n) section 191B`
