-- src:3518 | (q) section 191F (offences under this Part) is to be read as if—
-- src:3519 | (i) in subsection (2), “or section 190A applies” were omitted;
-- src:3520 | (ii) subsection (4A) were omitted;
-- src:3521 | (iii) for subsections (8) and (9) there were substituted—
-- src:3522 | (8) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) to (3) or (5) to (7) is liable—
-- src:3523 | (a) on summary conviction—
-- src:3524 | (i) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:3525 | (ii) in Scotland and Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding the statutory minimum;
-- src:3526 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to a fine.
-- src:3527 | (9) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (4) is liable—
-- src:3528 | (a) on summary conviction—
-- src:3529 | (i) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:3530 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum;
-- src:3531 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine, or both.
-- src:3532 | (iv) after subsection (9) there were inserted—
-- src:3533 | (10) A person is not guilty of an offence under this section if that person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence.
@ref sch 6B para 4(q) (src:3518-3533)
GIVETH A `sch 6B modification`
`sch 6B para 4(q) section 191F` MEANS
    `sch 6B modification` WITH
        `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS "191F"
        `how the limb treats the section` IS `sch 6B the section is read with the changes listed`
        `what the limb does to the section` IS "in subsection (2), 'or section 190A applies' omitted; subsection (4A) omitted; subsections (8) and (9) replaced; subsection (10) inserted"

-- Section 191F(8) and (9) as substituted by limb (q)(iii).  Here (9)(a)(ii) reads "statutory maximum" (FORK S6B-F3).
@ref sch 6B para 4(q)(iii) (src:3521-3531)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `sch 6B offence group`
      `the mode of conviction` IS A `sch 6B mode of conviction`
      `the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is convicted` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A `sch 6B penalty`
`sch 6B para 4(q)(iii) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offence` EQUALS `sch 6B an offence under section 191F(1) to (3) or (5) to (7)` AND `the mode of conviction` EQUALS `sch 6B conviction on indictment`
        THEN `sch 6B a fine`
        IF `the offence` EQUALS `sch 6B an offence under section 191F(1) to (3) or (5) to (7)` AND `the mode of conviction` EQUALS `sch 6B summary conviction` AND `the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is convicted` EQUALS `England and Wales`
        THEN `sch 6B a fine`
        IF `the offence` EQUALS `sch 6B an offence under section 191F(1) to (3) or (5) to (7)` AND `the mode of conviction` EQUALS `sch 6B summary conviction` AND (`the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is convicted` EQUALS `Scotland` OR `the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is convicted` EQUALS `Northern Ireland`)
        THEN `sch 6B a fine not exceeding the statutory minimum`
        IF `the offence` EQUALS `sch 6B an offence under section 191F(4)` AND `the mode of conviction` EQUALS `sch 6B conviction on indictment`
        THEN `sch 6B imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine, or both`
        IF `the offence` EQUALS `sch 6B an offence under section 191F(4)` AND `the mode of conviction` EQUALS `sch 6B summary conviction` AND `the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is convicted` EQUALS `England and Wales`
        THEN `sch 6B a fine`
        IF `the offence` EQUALS `sch 6B an offence under section 191F(4)` AND `the mode of conviction` EQUALS `sch 6B summary conviction` AND (`the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is convicted` EQUALS `Scotland` OR `the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is convicted` EQUALS `Northern Ireland`)
        THEN `sch 6B a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum`
        OTHERWISE `sch 6B the penalty is not stated in this paragraph` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the substituted subsections (8) and (9) state the penalty for subsections (1) to (7) of section 191F and no other

-- Section 191F(10), inserted by limb (q)(iv).
@ref sch 6B para 4(q)(iv) (src:3532-3533)
GIVEN `the person took all reasonable steps to avoid committing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 4(q)(iv) section 191F(10) the person is not guilty because the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person took all reasonable steps to avoid committing the offence` AND `the person exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not guilty of an offence under this section if that person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence." (marginal reading (a): a failed "if" is the text's no for this defence only; it does not say the person IS guilty)

-- src:3534 | (r) section 191G (interpretation) is to be read as if—
-- src:3535 | (i) the definitions of “the appropriate regulator”, “qualifying credit institution” and “UK authorised person” were omitted;
-- src:3536 | (ii) at the appropriate place there were inserted—
-- src:3537 | “registered cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider which is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.
@ref sch 6B para 4(r) (src:3534-3537)
GIVETH A `sch 6B modification`
`sch 6B para 4(r) section 191G` MEANS
    `sch 6B modification` WITH
        `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS "191G"
        `how the limb treats the section` IS `sch 6B the section is read with the changes listed`
        `what the limb does to the section` IS "the definitions of 'the appropriate regulator', 'qualifying credit institution' and 'UK authorised person' omitted; a definition of 'registered cryptoasset business' inserted"

@ref sch 6B para 4(r)(ii) (src:3537)
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is a custodian wallet provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 4(r)(ii) the business is a registered cryptoasset business within section 191G` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` OR `the business is a custodian wallet provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(2)`) AND `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registered cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider which is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)"

-- src:3538 | 5 Interpretation
-- src:3539 | In this Schedule—
@ref sch 6B para 5 (src:3538-3539)
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is a custodian wallet provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 5 the business is a cryptoasset business` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` OR `the business is a custodian wallet provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(2)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider;"

-- src:3540 | “cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider;
-- src:3541 | “cryptoasset exchange provider” has the meaning given by regulation 14A(1);
-- src:3542 | “custodian wallet provider” has the meaning given by regulation 14A(2);
-- The two terms of lines 3541 and 3542 point at regulation 14A, which another part encodes (SEAM S-K4/S-13 area); here they are pointers.
@ref sch 6B para 5 (src:3540-3542)
DECLARE `sch 6B para 5 defined term` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6B para 5 cryptoasset exchange provider`
    `sch 6B para 5 custodian wallet provider`

@ref sch 6B para 5 (src:3541-3542)
GIVEN term IS A `sch 6B para 5 defined term`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 6B para 5 the term has the meaning given by` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `sch 6B para 5 cryptoasset exchange provider` THEN "regulation 14A(1)"
    WHEN `sch 6B para 5 custodian wallet provider` THEN "regulation 14A(2)"

-- src:3543 | “registered cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider which is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A).
@ref sch 6B para 5 (src:3543)
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6B para 5 the business is a registered cryptoasset business` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` AND `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registered cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider which is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)." (a custodian wallet provider is not within this definition: FORK S6B-F1)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B, as guidance for hand-gathering only; paragraphs 1 and 3 and the lists of
-- paragraphs 2 and 4 each have their own functions above, option C): which set of changes applies to the business, and
-- how the applicable set treats a section of Part 12.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref sch 6B paras 1 and 3 (together)
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS A DATE
      `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `sch 6B the set of modifications`
`sch 6B paras 1 and 3 which set of modifications applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`sch 6B para 1 Part 12 of FSMA applies to the business with the modifications specified in paragraph 2` `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` `the date on which the business was included in the register` `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `sch 6B the modifications in paragraph 2`
        IF (`sch 6B para 3 Part 12 of FSMA applies to the business with the modifications specified in paragraph 4` `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` `the date on which the business was included in the register` `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `sch 6B the modifications in paragraph 4`
        OTHERWISE `sch 6B paragraphs 1 and 3 do not say that Part 12 applies` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs 1 and 3 apply Part 12 to one kind of business and are silent about every other

@ref sch 6B paras 2 and 4 (the tables of modifications together)
GIVEN modifications IS A LIST OF `sch 6B modification`
      `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6B treatment of a section`
`sch 6B a list of modifications treats the section as` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` EQUALS `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` AND r's `how the limb treats the section` EQUALS `sch 6B the section is disregarded`) modifications
        THEN `sch 6B the section is disregarded`
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` EQUALS `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` AND r's `how the limb treats the section` EQUALS `sch 6B the section is replaced by the text set out`) modifications
        THEN `sch 6B the section is replaced by the text set out`
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` EQUALS `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` AND r's `how the limb treats the section` EQUALS `sch 6B the section is read with the changes listed`) modifications
        THEN `sch 6B the section is read with the changes listed`
        OTHERWISE `sch 6B the section is not mentioned in the modifications` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a section that no limb mentions is neither said to apply nor said not to apply

@ref sch 6B paras 2 and 4 (the tables of modifications together)
GIVEN `the set of modifications that applies` IS A `sch 6B the set of modifications`
      `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6B treatment of a section`
`sch 6B paras 2 and 4 how the applicable set treats a section of Part 12 of FSMA` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the set of modifications that applies`
    WHEN `sch 6B the modifications in paragraph 2` THEN `sch 6B a list of modifications treats the section as` `sch 6B para 2 the modifications` `the section of Part 12 of FSMA`
    WHEN `sch 6B the modifications in paragraph 4` THEN `sch 6B a list of modifications treats the section as` `sch 6B para 4 the modifications` `the section of Part 12 of FSMA`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither paragraph 1 nor paragraph 3 applies Part 12 to the business, so there is no set of modifications to read
    WHEN `sch 6B paragraphs 1 and 3 do not say that Part 12 applies` THEN `sch 6B no modification applies because paragraphs 1 and 3 do not say that Part 12 applies`
